* ADG711 Quad SPST Analog Switch - single channel pass-through
* 2 V DC input -> 10 k load, 5 V single supply, switch commanded ON
*
* NOTE: ADG711 is the genuine vendor macromodel (no user-defined equivalent).
.include ADG711.cir
*
* Subcircuit pin order follows the 16-lead ADG711 pinout:
* 1:IN1 2:IN2 3:D2 4:S2 5:GND 6:VSS 7:S3 8:D3 9:IN3 10:IN4 11:D4 12:S4 13:VDD 14:D1 15:S1 16:VL
*
X1 CTRL1 CTRL2 D2 S2 0 VSS S3 D3 CTRL3 CTRL4 D4 S4 VDD OUT IN VL ADG711

*--- Supplies ---
VDD   VDD 0 DC 5
VSS   VSS 0 DC 0
VL    VL  0 DC 5

*--- Digital control: ADG711 switches are ON for logic LOW ---
VCTRL1 CTRL1 0 DC 0
VCTRL2 CTRL2 0 DC 5
VCTRL3 CTRL3 0 DC 5
VCTRL4 CTRL4 0 DC 5

*--- Signal path ---
VIN   IN  0 DC 2
RL    OUT 0 10k

*--- Terminate unused channels (avoid floating nodes) ---
RS2 S2 0 1G
RD2 D2 0 1G
RS3 S3 0 1G
RD3 D3 0 1G
RS4 S4 0 1G
RD4 D4 0 1G

*--- Analysis ---
.tran 10u 2m 0 10u
.meas TRAN vout_dc AVG V(OUT) FROM=1.5m TO=2m

.end
